## 4. Notes and limits

- **Kernel:** `openat2` requires Linux ≥ 5.6; on older kernels either fail fast on `ENOSYS` or fall back to a manual `openat(O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY)` component walk.
- **Concurrent rename out of the root:** regular files are created by a single `openat2` from the root fd (atomic); directory/symlink/hardlink creation uses a resolved parent fd plus `mkdirat`/`symlinkat`/`linkat`. A privileged process able to rename that directory out of the root between syscalls is outside the threat model. Run extraction in a private `0700` directory owned by the extractor (which also makes the pre-existing-hardlink-to-outside precondition impossible), or inside a user/mount namespace.
- **Never decode names.** `%2e%2e` is a literal filename; NUL bytes are rejected. Special files (device nodes, FIFOs) are refused rather than created.
- **Sparse:** `archive/tar` expands sparse members to logical size, so contents are byte-identical though physical holes are not reproduced; use `fallocate`/`SEEK_HOLE` if on-disk sparseness matters.

